Z||000002||BBBAD GT||09-03-2000||09:05 AM||||Just to give you reference, my V8 was from a 86-88 Caprice cop car.  Its a roller motor, with #193 casting heads (1.94 & 1.54 valves, centerbolt heads), and with only an Weiand Xcelerator and 600 Edelbrock carb, the rest bone stock, it made 207 rwhp.  I'm in the process of changing over to a Performer intake and maybe a 625 road demon carb.  I'm still trying to do some research on the longblock, but I think the compression is around low 9's (flat tops with valve reliefs per Chris).  I also think they were rated at 190 flywheel hp, but like I said, not sure.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/BBBAD_GT_SIG.gif">    <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||gixxer||09-03-2000||11:30 AM||||1964-65 Corvette fuel injected 327 CID, 375 HP (gross). <BR>1970 Corvette 350 CID LT1, carbed, 370 HP (gross). Probably about 300 HP net, and you might not pass the sniffer emissions test.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tryxalon||09-03-2000||02:03 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.gmpartsforsale.com/zz430_crate_engine.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.gmpartsforsale.com/zz430_crate_engine.htm</A> <P>or a little more reasonable: <BR> <A HREF="http://www.gmpartsforsale.com/zz430_crate_engine.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.gmpartsforsale.com/zz430_crate_engine.htm</A> <P>be prepared for a $4000-$5000 bill, plus hardware. <P><BR>Actually, I would think <A HREF="http://www.gmpartsforsale.com/ht43.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.gmpartsforsale.com/ht43.htm</A>  would save you about 3000 dollars and still allow you to attract the attention of your local law enforcement when ever you desire. ||||reg||1
